#: cheats.c:2805
msgid "Which memory to search. Work RAM is where most games keep lives, health and score; a Mega CD game can also use the CD's own memory, and a 32X game its SDRAM (the memory of the two SH-2 processors, codes 06aaaaaa:dd). Word RAM is searched in whichever mode the game has it (in its 1M mode only the half the main CPU has at that moment is seen). Changing it starts a new search."
msgstr ""

#: cheats.c:2806
msgid "Size:"
msgstr ""

#: cheats.c:2806
msgid "How big the value is: 1 byte (0 to 255: lives, ammo) or 2 bytes (0 to 65535: score, money). A 2-byte value is saved as two cheats. Changing it starts a new search."
msgstr ""

