#: dialogs.c:3652
msgid "  Open ROM... (Ctrl+O):"
msgstr ""

#: dialogs.c:3652
msgid "   Pick a game file to play: Mega Drive / Genesis (and Sega Pico, which uses the same file types), Master System, Game Gear, SG-1000, Mega CD, 32X (run by PicoDrive: needs picodrive_libretro.dll in the Plugins folder next to the program; some settings of the Genesis Plus GX core do not apply to those), or a .zip / .7z / .gz that holds one."
msgstr ""

#: dialogs.c:3652
msgid "  ROM Directory... (Ctrl+R):"
msgstr ""

#: dialogs.c:3652
msgid "   Shows the game browser for a folder of games. Double-click a game to play it, right-click for more choices (play with a saved state, cheats, cover image, clear the recently played list: it is grayed when there is nothing to clear); right-clicking empty space shows the same menu with the choices for a game grayed; with more than one ROM folder set, Open ROM Directory opens a list of them. Folders inside it are searched too (the Scan Subfolders box of the ROM Directories window, on by default)."
msgstr ""

#: dialogs.c:3652
msgid "  Recent Files:"
msgstr ""

#: dialogs.c:3652
msgid "   Your last games, each with its console on the right. If a game's file is gone, the program says so and asks whether to remove it from this list (and from Recently Played); the same question comes from the Recently Played group."
msgstr ""

#: dialogs.c:3652
msgid "  Change Disc...:"
msgstr ""

#: dialogs.c:3652
msgid "   A Mega CD command to swap the disc by hand, for games that do not ask for it themselves: pick the next disc's .cue or .chd file."
msgstr ""

#: dialogs.c:3652
msgid "  Run Mega CD BIOS:"
msgstr ""

#: dialogs.c:3652
msgid "   Starts the Mega CD's own BIOS with no disc (USA, Europe or Japan), to reach its CD player and settings screen. It needs bios_CD_U.bin, bios_CD_E.bin or bios_CD_J.bin in the BIOS folder. It is not added to the recent files or the played list."
msgstr ""

#: dialogs.c:3652
msgid "  Apply Patch...:"
msgstr ""

#: dialogs.c:3652
msgid "   Pick an .ips or .bps patch file (or a .zip or .7z that holds one) and it is applied in memory to the running game (the item is gray while no game runs), which is then started again from the patched copy: for translations and hacks. A .bps patch made for a different game is refused. The game file itself is not changed."
msgstr ""

#: dialogs.c:3652
msgid "  ROM Information...:"
msgstr ""

#: dialogs.c:3652
msgid "   The game's name, console, genre, whether it is a favorite, file size and location, the CRC32, the cartridge header (console name, type, titles, product code, region, copyright, supported controllers, save RAM), and the ROM size and checksum. Right-clicking the column titles offers Size All Columns to Fit."
msgstr ""

#: dialogs.c:3652
msgid "  Open Genesis Plus EX Folder:"
msgstr ""

#: dialogs.c:3652
msgid "   Opens the program folder: settings, saves, states, screenshots, recordings, cheats, covers and BIOS files."
msgstr ""

